-- title:
--   Archimedean twisted Harish-Chandra descent to the split torus
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be a finite Galois extension of number fields with $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by the integer powers of $\sigma$, and write $E = L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_{K,\infty}$ for the tensor product of $L$ with the infinite adele ring of $K$, with $\sigma$ acting on $E$ through the first factor (the ring map `sigmaTensor`, and `sigmaGL` its entrywise extension to $GL_2(E)$). Fix: a Haar measure $\nu_A$ on $\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty}^{\times}$; a Haar measure $\nu$ on $GL_2(E)$ for the Borel $\sigma$-algebra `glBorelOf`; an additive Haar measure $\mathrm{lam}$ on $E$; a Haar measure $\rho$ on $E^{\times}$; and a Haar measure $\kappa$ on the subgroup of $GL_2(E)$ obtained by pulling back, along `archIdentGL`, the intersection over the infinite places $w$ of $L$ of the preimages under `archComponent` of the subgroups of row isometries of $GL_2(L_w)$ (matrices of determinant of norm $1$ whose rows act isometrically on pairs $(x,y)$ in the sense of `IsRowIsometry`). Fix also a nonnegative Borel function $\beta$ on $GL_2(E)$ which is a section weight for the diagonal torus: for every pair $a = (a_1,a_2) \in (E^{\times})^2$, the integral over $(p_1,p_2) \in (\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty}^{\times})^2$ against $\nu_A \otimes \nu_A$ of $\beta$ evaluated at the product of the image under `toTensorGL` of $\mathrm{diag}(p_1,p_2)$ with $\mathrm{diag}(a_1,a_2)$ equals $1$. The assertion is the existence of a constant $c \in (0,\infty)$ (an element of $\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^{\infty}$ that is neither $0$ nor $\infty$) such that the following holds for all $\alpha, \beta' \in E^{\times}$ with $1 - N_{E/\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty}}(\beta'\alpha^{-1})$ a unit, all $\delta \in GL_2(E)$ whose matrix is $\mathrm{diag}(\alpha,\beta')$, all measures $\tau'$ on the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser of $\delta$ (with its Borel structure) which push forward the diagonal embedding, i.e. $\int g \, d\tau' = \int g(\mathrm{diag}(p_1,p_2))\, d(\nu_A \otimes \nu_A)$ for every $g : GL_2(E) \to \mathbb{C}$, the diagonal entries being taken through `toTensorGL`, all Borel $\varphi : GL_2(E) \to \mathbb{C}$ and all $w$ satisfying `IsTwistedSectionFnOn` for these data, that is, $w \geq 0$ is measurable with compact support and $\int_{t} w(tx) \, d\tau' = 1$ whenever $\varphi(x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(x)) \neq 0$: the product of $\prod_{v \mid \infty} \|(1 - N(\beta'\alpha^{-1}))_v\|^{\mathrm{mult}(v)}$, over the infinite places $v$ of $K$, with the $\nu$-integral of $\|\varphi(x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(x))\|_e \cdot w(x)$, equals $c$ times the iterated lower Lebesgue integral over $(a_1,a_2) \in (E^{\times})^2$ against $\rho \otimes \rho$ of $\beta(\mathrm{diag}(a_1,a_2))$ times the integral over $\xi \in E$ against $\mathrm{lam}$ of the $\kappa$-integral over $k$ of $\|\varphi\big(k^{-1}\,\mathrm{diag}(\alpha\,\sigma(a_1)a_1^{-1},\, \beta'\,\sigma(a_2)a_2^{-1})\, n(\xi)\, \sigma(k)\big)\|_e$, where $n(\xi)$ is the upper unipotent matrix `unipotentGL2` with entry $\xi$.
--
--   This is the archimedean twisted Harish-Chandra descent for $GL_2$: a twisted orbital integral over $GL_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_{K,\infty})$ at a regular diagonal $\delta$, weighted by a section function for the twisted centraliser, is rewritten, up to a positive finite constant and the archimedean Weyl discriminant factor $\prod_v \|1 - N(\beta'/\alpha)\|_v^{\mathrm{mult}(v)}$, as an iterated integral over the split torus, the unipotent radical and the maximal compact subgroup of row isometries. It feeds the comparison of twisted orbital integrals used in the archimedean base-change estimates, being cited by the bound on twisted orbital integrals along scalar multiples at the archimedean places.
